          <details class="guide-item">
            <summary class="guide-item__header">
              <span class="guide-item__number">01</span>
              <div class="guide-item__text">
                <span class="guide-item__title">Understanding UV Window Film Technology</span>
                <span class="guide-item__preview">How modern UV-blocking films protect interiors without sacrificing daylight.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="guide-item__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
              </div>
            </summary>
            <div class="guide-item__body">
              <p>Modern UV protection films use multi-layer technology to block up to 99% of ultraviolet radiation while maintaining optical clarity. Professional-grade films from manufacturers like 3M, LLumar, and Vista are engineered for the variable humidity and temperature conditions common in the Philadelphia region.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="guide-item">
            <summary class="guide-item__header">
              <span class="guide-item__number">02</span>
              <div class="guide-item__text">
                <span class="guide-item__title">Benefits of UV Protection for Philadelphia Properties</span>
                <span class="guide-item__preview">Why homes, storefronts, offices, and historic buildings benefit from UV film.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="guide-item__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
              </div>
            </summary>
            <div class="guide-item__body">
              <p>Philadelphia's diverse architecture — from Society Hill rowhouses to Chestnut Hill Victorians — features large windows that define the city's character but create ongoing UV exposure. Without protection, hardwood floors in Center City can fade noticeably within two to three years. Antique furniture, art collections, and historic finishes face cumulative damage that becomes visible only after it's already occurred.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="guide-item">
            <summary class="guide-item__header">
              <span class="guide-item__number">03</span>
              <div class="guide-item__text">
                <span class="guide-item__title">Types of UV Window Films We Offer</span>
                <span class="guide-item__preview">Clear, lightly tinted, and specialty film options for different spaces and goals.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="guide-item__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
              </div>
            </summary>
            <div class="guide-item__body">
              <p>We install films from 3M, LLumar, and Vista — each offering distinct advantages for Philadelphia properties. Clear UV films preserve original glass appearance for historic properties. Tinted variants add heat rejection for south- and west-facing windows. Manufacturer warranties vary; we provide complete documentation and warranty registration for every installation.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="guide-item">
            <summary class="guide-item__header">
              <span class="guide-item__number">04</span>
              <div class="guide-item__text">
                <span class="guide-item__title">Performance Metrics & Specifications</span>
                <span class="guide-item__preview">What UV rejection, visible light transmission, and related performance numbers really mean.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="guide-item__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
              </div>
            </summary>
            <div class="guide-item__body">
              <p>Key metrics include UV Rejection (the percentage of UV rays blocked), Visible Light Transmission (how much natural light passes through), and Solar Heat Gain Coefficient (heat rejection). Quality films typically achieve 99% UV rejection while maintaining 70–80% visible light transmission in clear configurations. All films we install carry independent certification and manufacturer warranties.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="guide-item">
            <summary class="guide-item__header">
              <span class="guide-item__number">05</span>
              <div class="guide-item__text">
                <span class="guide-item__title">Applications Across Philadelphia</span>
                <span class="guide-item__preview">Where UV protection film works best, from rowhomes to retail spaces.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="guide-item__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
              </div>
            </summary>
            <div class="guide-item__body">
              <p>UV protection film works across Philadelphia's diverse property types. Center City high-rises with floor-to-ceiling windows, South Philly townhouses with south-facing exposures, and Manayunk hillside homes each have distinct UV patterns. Historic properties in Rittenhouse, Chestnut Hill, and Society Hill often cannot replace original windows — film adds protection without altering irreplaceable historic glass. Commercial spaces throughout the city benefit from protecting employees, merchandise, and furnishings from UV exposure.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="guide-item">
            <summary class="guide-item__header">
              <span class="guide-item__number">06</span>
              <div class="guide-item__text">
                <span class="guide-item__title">Our Professional Installation Process</span>
                <span class="guide-item__preview">What to expect from consultation through final installation.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="guide-item__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
              </div>
            </summary>
            <div class="guide-item__body">
              <p>Our process starts with an on-site assessment at your Philadelphia property. We evaluate window orientations, exposure levels, and your protection priorities. Residential installations typically complete in a single day. Commercial projects schedule around your building operations, often evenings or weekends. Our crews are manufacturer-certified and experienced with historic Philadelphia window configurations.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="guide-item">
            <summary class="guide-item__header">
              <span class="guide-item__number">07</span>
              <div class="guide-item__text">
                <span class="guide-item__title">Warranty, Maintenance & Lifespan</span>
                <span class="guide-item__preview">How long UV film lasts and how to care for it properly.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="guide-item__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
              </div>
            </summary>
            <div class="guide-item__body">
              <p>Quality UV films installed by professionals typically last 15–20 years with minimal maintenance — regular glass cleaning with soft cloths and standard solutions maintains optical clarity. Manufacturer warranties typically range from 10 years to lifetime coverage for residential installations, covering film degradation, bubbling, and peeling when properly maintained.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="guide-item">
            <summary class="guide-item__header">
              <span class="guide-item__number">08</span>
              <div class="guide-item__text">
                <span class="guide-item__title">Cost & Return on Investment</span>
                <span class="guide-item__preview">What professional UV film installation typically costs and the value it delivers.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="guide-item__toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
              </div>
            </summary>
            <div class="guide-item__body">
              <p>Professional UV protection film installation in the Philadelphia area typically costs $8–$15 per square foot depending on film selection and window configuration. We provide detailed quotes following on-site assessments so you know the exact cost before work begins. Value comes through protecting hardwood floors ($8–$15/sq ft to replace), reducing fading damage over time, and heat rejection that may also help improve comfort during Philadelphia's warm months.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
